    tools: add three standing pre-insert gates (spill sweep, boxtitle check, PDF edge scan)
    
    W47 proofread found three blind spots in the existing gates
    (run-log 2026-11-11): check_creambox only inspects texts whose
    baseline falls inside a cream rect; box titles had no width check
    (it-de P1 cifre title overran its box by +138.5px); delivered PDFs
    had no raster edge scan. These three read-only scripts close them:
    
    - tools/spill_sweep.py: whole-line cream-box spill sweep (60px
      neighbourhood, same-flow adjudication: same size + same x +
      line-advance match; nominal advance 1.40x size when a box holds
      a single line of that size).
    - tools/boxtitle_check.py: per-title PIL true-ink width vs box
      width, with core + backup adjudication (STRADDLE rule); falls
      back to the single-CJK-font model for the old-generation
      core-ja / core-ko svglib.
    - tools/pdf_edge_scan.py: delivered print PDF rendered at
      200dpi (MuPDF), 3px outer band must be ink-free.
    
    All three validated on the full 130-edition W47 set; results in
    hidden_files/w47/Reports-preinsert/new-gates-130.md (21 defects:
    spill 1, boxtitle 18, edge 2).

